Dear Mr Mitul Jain,

2nd Edition of CII Digital Green Manufacturing Summit 2026
Theme: "Digital Green Manufacturing 2.0
Innovate, Integrate, Impact - Scaling Sustainable Manufacturing for Global =
Competitiveness"
7 October 2026: Chennai

Manufacturing continues to be a key driver of economic growth across South =
India, with industries increasingly adopting sustainable practices and smar=
t manufacturing technologies to enhance efficiency, resilience, and global =
competitiveness. As organizations pursue their sustainability and decarboni=
zation goals, the convergence of Industry 4.0 technologies with green manuf=
acturing is creating new opportunities for innovation, resource optimizatio=
n and business growth.

Building on the success of its first edition, the 2nd Edition of the CII Di=
gital Green Manufacturing Summit 2026, themed "Digital Green Manufacturing =
2.0: Innovate, Integrate, Impact - Scaling Sustainable Manufacturing for Gl=
obal Competitiveness," will be held on 7 October 2026 at Chennai. The Summi=
t will focus on accelerating the transition towards greener, smarter, and m=
ore competitive manufacturing.

The conference will be chaired by Mr Unnikrishnan AR, Managing Director, Sa=
int-Gobain India Pvt Ltd.

The key session themes at this summit include:

v  Intelligent Technologies for Sustainable Operations: AI, IoT, Digital Tw=
ins and Automation for Resource Efficiency
v  Nurturing Green Skills & Building Capacity: From R&D to End of Lifecycle=
 Management
v  Fireside Chat Session on Leaders Dialogue: Accelerating the Twin Transit=
ion for Resilient and Competitive Growth
v  From Vision to Value: Scaling Digital Green Manufacturing through Innova=
tion and Stakeholder Collaboration

The Summit is expected to attract a distinguished gathering of over 150 par=
ticipants including - Industry Leaders & CXOs, Policy Makers, Sustainabilit=
y and Operations Leaders, Digital Transformation Experts, Technology Provid=
ers, Startups, Industry Associations, and Academia. The event will serve as=
 a platform for key stakeholders to exchange insights, showcase best practi=
ces and drive collaboration for advancing digital and sustainable manufactu=
ring.

Key Speakers (Confirmed):
*       Mr Simranjeet Singh Kahlon, IAS, Managing Director, Tamil Nadu Skil=
l Development Corporation (TNSDC)
*       Mr Unnikrishnan AR, Conference Chairman & Managing Director, Saint-=
Gobain India Pvt Ltd
*       Mr M Ponnuswami, Founder, Chairman & Managing Director, Pon Pure Ch=
emicals Group
*       Ms Amudhavalli Ranganathan, Director - Ecommerce, New Initiatives, =
CavinKare Pvt Ltd
*       Ms Gowri Kailasam, Executive Director, Rane (Madras) Limited
*       Mr A Prashanth, Managing Director, Bosch Mobility Platform & Soluti=
ons Pvt Ltd
*       Mr P V Kiran Ananth, Executive Director - Energy Efficiency, Renewa=
ble Energy and Green Entrepreneurship, CII-GBC
*       Mr Nikhil S Tambe, CEO - The Energy Consortium, IIT Madras
*       Mr Murali Chandrahasan, Senior Director & Head - Intelligent Indust=
ry, Capgemini Invent India
*       Mr Rahul Dev Mandal, CEO & Co-Founder, Nebeskie Labs
*       Mr Alok Verma, Head - Corporate Strategy & ESG, Ashok Leyland Ltd



*       Mr Sanjay Loganathan, GM - Special Projects & Sustainability, Isuzu=
 Motors India
*       Ms Anju Mary K, Independent Director & Sustainability Consultant
*       Mr Shaji Namath, Founder & Director, XLR Partners
*       Mr Sunil David, Digital Technology Consultant, Ex-Regional Director=
- IOT, AT&T India
... and other eminent industry leaders

